{"kind":"request","text":"S1-F: three follow-ups from the S1 review, one small head.\n\nChecker approval c6fcf62e left three items for a later head. None\nchanges what S1 landed as main 221e11c3. The source request is\n8bd2c9d2.\n\n1. Document the creation-table limit. State in section 7 of\n   docs/security/entry-points.md that the creation table holds 8,192\n   windows for an hour and one address key opens at most 31. About\n   265 distinct IPv4 addresses or IPv6 /64s fill the table. After\n   that, every new identity shares 10 creations an hour until rows\n   expire. Callers that already hold windows keep them. A sender with\n   one IPv6 /48 can reach that state.\n2. Charge the address for a refused found intent. submit applies the\n   found window only when boundedServingIntent succeeds. A found\n   intent over 1 MiB, or one that fails the strict parse, reaches the\n   target with no found charge. Charge the address window in that\n   case too, so the rule reads: every found submit charges the\n   address.\n3. Simplify the accounting call. Give creation its own method if\n   that removes the five-argument call. Do this only if the head\n   gets smaller. If it does not, say so in the request and leave it.\n\nDo not change the overflow key in this head. A coarser key for the\noverflow decision is a separate decision. I will rule on it before\nthe live window.\n\nTests: one test for item 2 that fails without the charge. Item 1\nneeds the entry-points check to pass. Item 3 needs no new test.\n\nOrder: after S4 and the cutover head. This head takes no gate slot\nfrom either.","body":{"conditions":"One small head on main with the named tests. Gate once. Checker review before landing.","target_head":"221e11c33428068e0b95ffaa30aa0d294186b3c0","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}